<?xml version='1.0' encoding='UTF-8'?>
<catalogue xmlns="http://www.battlescribe.net/schema/catalogueSchema" id="orks-main-0000-0001" name="LI - Orks" revision="1" battleScribeVersion="2.03" library="false" gameSystemId="28d4-bd2e-4858-ece6" gameSystemRevision="130" type="catalogue">
  <readme>Orks (Xenos) faction for Horus Heresy 2.0. Based on Xenologica 2e - Waaaaagh! The Orks! (v2.2).

Faction: Xenos, Orks sub-faction

Alliance Levels:
- Sworn Brothers: None
- Fellow Warriors: None
- Distrusted Allies: Agents of the Warmaster, Legiones Astartes, Imperial Army, unlisted Xenos
- By the Emperor's Order: Agents of the Imperium, Mechanicum, Daemons of the Ruinstorm, T'au Empire, Leagues of Votann

Imperial Militia Provenance: Digganobz (Xenos faction, Fellow Warriors with Orks, Stubborn within 12" of Orks units)</readme>

  <categoryEntries>
    <categoryEntry id="orks-cat0-0001-0001" name="Orks Sub-type" hidden="false" />
    <categoryEntry id="orks-cat0-mob0-0001" name="Mob Sub-type" hidden="false">
      <rules>
        <rule id="orks-rule-mob0-cat1" name="Mob Sub-type" hidden="false">
          <description>The following rules apply to all models with the Mob sub-type:
• A unit that contains a majority of models with the Mob sub-type can substitute the amount of models in its unit for its Leadership characteristic whenever it takes a Morale or Pinning check, up to a maximum of 10.
• Whilst a unit contains 11 or more models with the Mob sub-type, all models in that unit gain the Fearless special rule.
• A model with the Bulky (X) special rule counts as a number of models equal to the number listed in brackets in its Bulky special rule for the purpose of the Mob sub-type.</description>
        </rule>
      </rules>
    </categoryEntry>
    <categoryEntry id="orks-cat0-rams-0001" name="Ramshackle Sub-type" hidden="false">
      <rules>
        <rule id="orks-rule-rams-cat1" name="Ramshackle Sub-type" hidden="false">
          <description>The following rules apply to all models with the Ramshackle sub-type:
• A model with the Ramshackle sub-type has a 6+ Invulnerable Save. That save may not be taken against Wounds, Glancing Hits or Penetrating Hits inflicted by weapons with the Ordnance or Destroyer type.
• When a Vehicle model with this Sub-type suffers the Explodes result from the Vehicle Damage Table (but not the Crashes and Burn result), roll a D6 and apply the result on the following table:
 -1-2: Skrrronk: Replace that result with the Immobilized result.
 -3-4: Vlam!: Resolve the Explodes result as normal, except the Strength of any Hits inflicted as part of the Explodes result is reduced to 4.
 -5-6: Carreen: The model can make a Move of up to D6+6&quot; before resolving the Explodes result.
• When a model with this Sub-type that has a Wounds characteristic loses its last Wound, but before it is removed as a casualty, each model, friendly and enemy, within D6&quot; suffers a Hit with AP- and a Strength equal to the Toughness value of the model.</description>
        </rule>
      </rules>
    </categoryEntry>
    <categoryEntry id="orks-cat0-prmk-0001" name="Prime-Ork Unit Type" hidden="false">
      <rules>
        <rule id="orks-rule-prmk-cat1" name="Prime-Ork Unit Type" hidden="false">
          <description>The following rules apply to all models with the Prime-Ork unit type:
• Prime-Orks are counted as Primarchs during army creation, and count against your Lords of War and Primarch allowance. In addition, for the purpose of any special rule that affects or has additional effects that target models with the Primarch Unit Type, a model with the Prime-Ork Unit Type is considered to have the Primarch Unit Type.
• All Prime-Orks have the following special rules: Eternal Warrior, Fearless, It Will Not Die (5+), Bulky (6), Independent Character, and Relentless. In addition, all models with the Prime-Ork unit type always count as Character models.
• Prime-Orks are not affected by special rules that negatively modify their Characteristics (other than Wounds) and, in addition, Prime-Orks always resolve Snap Shots at their normal BS.
• Any Hits inflicted by a Prime-Ork, as part of either Shooting Attacks or in close combat, are allocated by the Prime-Ork's controlling player and not the controlling player of the target unit. These Hits should form a separate Wound Pool.
• If an army includes any Prime-Ork models, then one of those models must be chosen as the army's Warlord.</description>
        </rule>
      </rules>
    </categoryEntry>
    <categoryEntry id="orks-cat0-gprm-0001" name="Gargantuan Prime-Ork Unit Type" hidden="false">
      <rules>
        <rule id="orks-rule-gprm-cat1" name="Gargantuan Prime-Ork Unit Type" hidden="false">
          <description>The following rules apply to all models with the Gargantuan Prime-Ork unit type:
• Models with the Gargantuan Prime-Ork Unit Type follow all rules for the Gargantuan and Prime-Ork unit Types, except they do not have the Independent Character special rule and are not Character models.
• For the purposes of any special rule that affects or has additional effects that target models with the Gargantuan or Prime-Ork Unit Type, a model with the Gargantuan Prime-Ork Unit Type is considered to have the Gargantuan and Prime-Ork Unit Types.</description>
        </rule>
      </rules>
    </categoryEntry>
  </categoryEntries>

  <selectionEntries>
  </selectionEntries>

